    "description": "Measures stereotypical bias in English language models on gender, profession, race, and religion. Each item is a context with stereotype, anti-stereotype, and unrelated options (intrasentence fill-in or intersentence continuation). Cards report language modeling score (LMS), stereotype score (SS; 50 is ideal), and idealized CAT (ICAT).",
    "summary": "Measures how often the model prefers stereotypes over neutral or opposite choices about gender, job, race, and religion.",
